A||N||2||Esaud||Trouble accessing accelerator pedal - bigfoot||||5||
Z||000000||Esaud||06-24-2001||12:14 PM||||Is there a modification that can be made to allow better access to the accelerator pedal due to lack of space between brake pedal and console wall?  My foot does not have enough room for my 85 GT V/6 4 speed.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodney||06-24-2001||02:12 PM||||Here is the responce I emailed him on this. <P><BR>I have the same problem but I have not seen anyone do<BR>anything to make it better. I have an extra layer of<BR>carpet also making it worse. Maybe pull the carpet back<BR>and trim the under pad next to the pedal. Then contact<BR>cement the carpet to the wall. There may be a plastic<BR>piece in there. That could be trimed some?? I should do<BR>this to my car also! I mostly drive in bare feet so it<BR>is not a problem. Only when I have to wear shoes.<P><BR>I put this on list of to do things. I'm sure I can make mine better. Possibly the plastic part that holds the cruise control ECM can be trimmed some also?? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-24-2001||03:32 PM||||One posible solution... Only if you have an automatic. I don't think you have enough room to try this with a clutch.<P>get a spare brake pedal, don't do this to your existing one just in case it doesn't work out.<P>heat it in a couple spots and bend it so the pad is more to the left. Better to cold bend it in a press if it will take it. That won't change the hardness of the metal.<P>Keep in mind this will shorten the pedal slightly. Allot depending how you bend it. this will increase pedal effort by a related amount. As long as you make 2 slight bends it should not be too bad.<P>Optionally, you could cut the pedal and alter it. The welds have to be perfect though. Otherwise it could break during a panic stop.||||reg||1
